---
import {
  ASSIGNEE_CSV,
  ASSIGNEE_CSV_NAME,
  ASSIGNEE_TOTALS,
  RUN_REPORT_ANSWER,
  RUN_REPORT_CALL,
  REPORTS_MANUAL_PATH,
} from '@lib/features/project-reports';

const ACCESS = [
  {
    title: 'Only issues you could open.',
    body: 'A report is scoped to the projects you can read before anything is counted. Projects you are not a member of and deleted issues never reach a bar, a total or a CSV.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Every role can view and export.',
    body: 'Observers included. Anyone who can see a report can download its CSV, with the same numbers on screen.',
  },
  {
    title: 'An agent sees no more than its token.',
    body: 'Through MCP, a report is limited further to the projects the access token allows, and needs the issues:read scope.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Worked out when you open it.',
    body: 'A report shows the time it was computed and does not refresh itself. A result is kept for at most five minutes, and any change in the organisation starts a fresh one.',
  },
];
---

<section id="same-numbers" class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="same-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[680px]">
      <h2 id="same-title" class="h2">
        One table for the chart, the CSV and your agent.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        Report definitions live on the server, and the web app, the CSV export and the <code>run_report</code> tool all
        call the same one. These are the Sprint 08 figures from the chart above, as a download and as an agent reads
        them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 md:mt-14 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 panel overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bar-head">
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Export CSV</span>
          <span class="mono text-xs text-fg-2 truncate">{ASSIGNEE_CSV_NAME}</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="block-pre" tabindex="0" aria-label={`Contents of ${ASSIGNEE_CSV_NAME}`}>{ASSIGNEE_CSV}</pre>
        <p class="foot">
          Shares are of the {ASSIGNEE_TOTALS.counted} the bars add up to. The Total row counts each issue once, so it
          reads {ASSIGNEE_TOTALS.issues}.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 panel overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bar-head">
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Your agent asks</span>
          <span class="mono text-xs text-fg-2">run_report</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="block-pre" tabindex="0" aria-label="The run_report call">{RUN_REPORT_CALL}</pre>
        <div class="bar-head border-t border-line">
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">and reads</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="block-pre" tabindex="0" aria-label="The run_report answer">{RUN_REPORT_ANSWER}</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-fg-2 max-w-[70ch]">
      An agent names the report and its choices the way you do, and when a report is empty it is told which filter to
      drop.{' '}
      <a class="link" href="/features/mcp-ai-agents">
        MCP and AI agents
        <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
          →
        </span>
      </a>
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14 md:mt-20 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <h3 class="h2 text-[24px] md:text-[28px]">Reports follow project permissions.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-4 max-w-[40ch]">
          A report never reveals an issue you could not open directly.{' '}
          <a class="link" href={REPORTS_MANUAL_PATH}>
            Reports manual
            <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:col-start-6 grid md:grid-cols-2 border-t border-line">
        {ACCESS.map(item => (
          <div class="module border-b border-line">
            <h4 class="h3">{item.title}</h4>
            <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .bar-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    min-height: 40px;
    padding: 6px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .bar-head > :last-child {
    margin-left: auto;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .bar-head > :only-child {
    margin-left: 0;
  }
  .block-pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    background: var(--bg-app);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 20px;
    color: var(--text);
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .block-pre:focus-visible {
    border-radius: 0;
    box-shadow: inset var(--focus-ring);
  }
  .foot {
    padding: 12px 16px 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 18px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
